  Placement: 1
  CardStory: "I was never devout. I believed, of course, because what else is there
    to do? I saw one of Her holy wreaths, as a child, on the altars of the Great
    Cathedral. I prayed, because what else is there to do?\r\n\r\nBut not like now.
    Never like now. As I run barefoot through the hallways of this broken place,
    being made sport of by men who cast away everything that made them civilised.
    As I fall and scrape my knees to the sound of their mocking laughs. I pray, truly
    pray for Her to save me. \r\n\r\nAnd she does.\r\n\r\nA single black thorn, emerging
    from the ground, inches from my bloodied, sweaty face. I know the process. Every
    child is taught, even if most never go through it. Slow, methodical, pressed
    upon skin to carefully grow within the supplicant\u2019s body.\r\n\r\nI swallow
    it whole."
